WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.311 --> 00:00:01.740
- [Ben] Okay, fourth rule for debating:

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.192
Frame the debate properly.

00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:04.025
So, you see this all the time.

00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:05.919
People frame the debate
completely incorrectly.

00:00:05.919 --> 00:00:07.959
So in every debate the left
is trying to frame the debate

00:00:07.959 --> 00:00:08.792
in a particular way.

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:10.281
So let's take an example from
the last couple of weeks.

00:00:10.281 --> 00:00:12.052
The left was trying to frame this issue

00:00:12.052 --> 00:00:14.685
on the border as Donald
Trump is separating children

00:00:14.685 --> 00:00:15.895
from their parents.

00:00:15.895 --> 00:00:17.782
The Trump administration
responded by saying

00:00:17.782 --> 00:00:19.203
"Well the reason we're separating children

00:00:19.203 --> 00:00:20.863
from their parents is
because it was a deterrent."

00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:22.527
That was the original response.

00:00:22.527 --> 00:00:24.285
That is the worst response ever.

00:00:24.285 --> 00:00:25.738
That is a bad response.

00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:28.576
The way that they should
have responded is by saying

00:00:28.576 --> 00:00:30.293
first of all that's
not true, we don't want

00:00:30.293 --> 00:00:31.467
to separate children from their parents.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.188
The Ninth Circuit Court
of Appeals rules that

00:00:33.188 --> 00:00:34.021
if we arrest people,

00:00:34.021 --> 00:00:36.055
we have to separate
children from their parents

00:00:36.055 --> 00:00:37.634
so if you don't like
that rule, we can go back

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.900
to the Obama era rule where
we detained everybody.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.600
Which is of course what
Trump is doing now.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.777
Right now Trump has said

00:00:42.777 --> 00:00:43.867
"Okay, well fine we'll detain everybody."

00:00:43.867 --> 00:00:45.034
Then the left goes "Well it's nazi-esque

00:00:45.034 --> 00:00:47.198
when you separate parents and children

00:00:47.198 --> 00:00:48.593
and it's nazi-esque when
you keep them together,

00:00:48.593 --> 00:00:50.023
because their end argument is

00:00:50.023 --> 00:00:51.199
they just want everybody released.

00:00:51.199 --> 00:00:53.506
But how you frame the debate
originally really matters

00:00:53.506 --> 00:00:55.116
in a major way.

00:00:55.116 --> 00:00:57.184
Now President Trump actually
is typically very good

00:00:57.184 --> 00:00:58.260
at framing the debate.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.888
President Trump actually
is great at picking

00:01:00.888 --> 00:01:03.903
a frame that works for
him and then moving on it

00:01:03.903 --> 00:01:05.252
so instinctively he has
a good feel for this.

00:01:05.252 --> 00:01:06.973
So on the immigration debate
when he says immediately,

00:01:06.973 --> 00:01:08.195
"Democrats want open borders."

00:01:08.195 --> 00:01:09.346
That is a good way to frame the debate

00:01:09.346 --> 00:01:10.913
because that is actually the debate,

00:01:10.913 --> 00:01:12.237
and Democrats don't
want to have that debate

00:01:12.237 --> 00:01:13.431
because they lose that debate.

00:01:13.431 --> 00:01:15.460
They want to have the
you're mean to kids debate.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:16.862
The problem with this
latest roll-out is that

00:01:16.862 --> 00:01:18.078
if they'd rolled it out with

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.424
you want open borders, we
don't want open borders,

00:01:20.424 --> 00:01:22.290
the reasons parents are
being separated from kids

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.891
is because that is the current law,

00:01:23.891 --> 00:01:24.991
we'd like the law to change and we're

00:01:24.991 --> 00:01:27.022
calling on Congress to do so.

00:01:27.022 --> 00:01:29.076
That would have been the way
to frame the debate totally.

00:01:29.076 --> 00:01:30.774
They're coming around to it,
it's just a little bit late.

00:01:30.774 --> 00:01:32.082
So it's all about framing the debate.

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:33.343
Whenever you're debating anybody,

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:34.369
and this is true for any topic,

00:01:34.369 --> 00:01:35.940
the left has a series
of frames on the debate.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.537
Whenever they talk about
global warming for example,

00:01:37.537 --> 00:01:38.525
they'll frame the debate as

00:01:38.525 --> 00:01:40.565
you don't care whether
there's global warming,

00:01:40.565 --> 00:01:42.724
or you are a global warming denier.

00:01:42.724 --> 00:01:43.713
The way you should actually
frame the debate is

00:01:43.713 --> 00:01:46.565
okay what are your
solutions to global warming?

00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:49.419
The reason being that, I
assume there are very few

00:01:49.419 --> 00:01:50.981
climate scientists in the room.

00:01:50.981 --> 00:01:52.311
I'm not a climate scientist.

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:53.714
I don't know that much about

00:01:53.714 --> 00:01:56.741
the reactivity of the
atmosphere to carbon emissions,

00:01:56.741 --> 00:01:59.299
but even if I accept the IPCC estimate

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:00.463
that by the end of the century,

00:02:00.463 --> 00:02:02.124
the average climate across
planet Earth will rise

00:02:02.124 --> 00:02:03.770
something on the order of
seven degrees Fahrenheit,

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:04.691
that does not suggest that

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:07.661
massive government interventionism
is necessarily the fix.

00:02:07.661 --> 00:02:10.073
In fact, it's a pretty good
chance that it's not the fix,

00:02:10.073 --> 00:02:12.540
considering that if the Kyoto
Protocols or the Paris Accords

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.434
were implemented right now,

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:16.586
it would barely lower
the temperature at all

00:02:16.586 --> 00:02:18.173
according to their own best estimate.

00:02:18.173 --> 00:02:19.921
Once you get into that, the
left has nothing to say.

00:02:19.921 --> 00:02:22.136
They'd prefer to stick in the
area where you're an ignoramus

00:02:22.136 --> 00:02:23.240
who doesn't know anything about science

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.230
and you hate science.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.099
So it's all about reframing
every debate, right?

00:02:26.099 --> 00:02:28.387
On abortion it's about not
arguing about women's choice

00:02:28.387 --> 00:02:30.109
it's about arguing whether
this is a human life or not

00:02:30.109 --> 00:02:32.976
because that really is the
only debate that matters.

00:02:32.976 --> 00:02:33.941
Alright, I'm not against women's choice,

00:02:33.941 --> 00:02:35.257
women can choose to do whatever they want

00:02:35.257 --> 00:02:38.202
just they can't kill babies
because I can't kill babies,

00:02:38.202 --> 00:02:39.799
because no one can kill babies.

00:02:39.799 --> 00:02:41.328
So, it's all about where you
choose to frame the debate.

